- the blocks end up held within the storage of 0;
- storage 4 and its parts die;
- places 7 and 8 die;
- 7 and 8 are released.
The theorem checks only the last one (`¬ fc4.Active 7 ∧ ¬ fc4.Active 8`), plus `¬ fc4.Active 4`. Authority 4 is the arena's internal root authority (holder place 0, footprint [5, 6]), not the place 4, so it says nothing about places being usable. No declaration mentions `fc4.Usable` or the holders after the two transfers: `grep -n 'fc1\|fc4'` shows only the two defs and the theorem. All the facts are true by `decide`. The first verification treated the same kind of fact, true but with no witness in the module, as a confirmed defect (verdicts 7 and 14), so this is an unsupported claim in a new docstring and report passage.

